  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/ExtendedDnS.owl#objective">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Na4eaa9abbff24a5ea0665a7e6564b08d"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dlp/ExtendedDnS.owl#modal-description"/>
    <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The purpose of an agent, either physical or social. It is different from a desire or goal, because it is independent from the cognitive state of a particular physical agent.
In practice, an agent (physical or social) may aim at realizing an objective even though the realizing situation conflicts with a goal-situation of the same agent.
In 'private' plans of a physical agent,  realizing situations usually coincide with goal-situations.
Different cases occur with plans endorsed by social agents like organizations, institutions, etc.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
